dflash-seed: per-request seeded sampling on the SGLang DFLASH verify/accept path (mirrors EAGLE)
=================================================================================================
Target: SGLang @1cf2b8c54d81 (= the contest image's sglang 0.5.6.post3.dev9160+g1cf2b8c54; local copy
= that image's python/ tree).
STATUS: PREPARED, NOT APPLIED to any submission. Apply in a container only via apply_seed_shim.sh.
Apply by hand: repo root `git apply -p1 dflash_seed.patch`; installed tree `patch -p2 -d <site-packages> < dflash_seed.patch`.

WHY. With T>0 the DFLASH verify draws its rejection coins and its final-token coin from torch.rand, i.e. from the
one global CUDA generator shared by every request in the batch, consumed in batch order
(dflash_utils.py:886-900 when uniform_samples is None; dflash_worker_v2.py:2028 never passes coins). The OpenAI
"seed" reaches SamplingBatchInfo.sampling_seed only under --enable-deterministic-inference, and even then only
EAGLE uses it (eagle_utils.py:583-643 _seeded_verify_coins). So two runs with the same seed diverge at the
first free token (CRITIC_B E2: 0/2,173 drafts identical, first differing byte p50 = 106).

WHAT. 3 files, 6 hunks:
 H1 sampling_batch_info.py  `import os` (needed by H2).
 H2 sampling_batch_info.py  from_schedule_batch: new local `seeded_sampling = enable_deterministic or
    env SGLANG_DFLASH_SEEDED_SAMPLING == "1"`. Default ("0" / unset) = stock behaviour exactly.
 H3 sampling_batch_info.py  build the per-request sampling_seed tensor when `seeded_sampling` (was:
    only when enable_deterministic). Requests without a seed get 42, the stock deterministic-mode default.
    Side effect (intended): the normal Sampler, which in DFLASH only samples the FIRST token after
    prefill/extend, now uses multinomial_with_seed(seed, position). That sampler asserts
    sampling_seed is None on the flashinfer backend when top_k/top_p are used, so H2's env mode REQUIRES
    `--sampling-backend pytorch` (apply_seed_shim.sh refuses to start without it, unless
    --enable-deterministic-inference is given, which forces pytorch itself). Cost: the pytorch sampler
    sorts the vocab, but only for one token per request (decode tokens all come from the verify path).
    Also stock: seeded sampling refuses min_p > 0 (sampler.py:590 assert); our coder uses min_p 0.
 H4 dflash_utils.py  new helper dflash_seeded_verify_coins(sampling_info, seq_lens, draft_token_num,
    device) -> (coins[bs, draft_token_num], final_coins[bs]) from EAGLE's own _seeded_verify_coins
    (murmur_hash32(seed, seq_len, column) / 2^32-1, clamped < 1), or (None, None) when no sampling_seed.
    Reusing the EAGLE function (lazy import; eagle_utils is already imported by the scheduler) keeps one
    coin scheme in the codebase. compute_dflash_sampling_correct_drafts_and_bonus is NOT changed: it
    already accepts uniform_samples / uniform_samples_for_final_sampling and falls back to torch.rand on None.
 H5 dflash_worker_v2.py  import the helper.
 H6 dflash_worker_v2.py  in the T>0 chain-verify branch only, compute the seeded coins with
    seq_lens = prefix_lens (the committed length before this verify, the same tensor the greedy Triton
    path uses for new_seq_lens; EAGLE uses batch.seq_lens at the same point) and pass them in.

EXACTNESS (same distribution as unseeded, just seeded). The accept rule, the target probs, draft_probs = 0
(target-only chain verify) and the kernel tree_speculative_sampling_target_only are untouched; only the
source of the U[0,1) coins changes. Speculative sampling is exact iff, at each step, the coins are U[0,1),
mutually independent and independent of the draft tokens and of earlier coins of the same request. The hash
key (seed, prefix_len, column) satisfies this: columns 0..B-1 are the per-position coins and column B the
final coin (distinct keys within a step); prefix_len strictly increases every step (each verify commits
>= 1 token), so no key repeats across steps; the first-token sampler uses (seed, L-1, vocab id) with
L = prompt length, while every verify uses prefix_len >= L, so no key is shared with it either. Coins are
quantized to 2^-32 then rounded to float32 (torch.rand float32 is 2^-24 grained), clamped below 1.0 (the
EAGLE fix: a 1.0 coin can pick a zero-probability token). Residual non-uniformity ~1e-7 (float32), the
same as upstream's EAGLE/deterministic path. Requests that share a seed (seed only, any prompt) share the
coin stream; the pipeline gives every draft its own seed (task.seed + seed_offset + k).

NOT COVERED (by design, keep the patch minimal):
 - The DFlash2 "selector" drafter (models/dflash.py DFlash2DraftModel; dflash_worker_v2.py:246 in-graph
   philox self.uniforms.uniform_(), :973 torch.rand, :1001 accept_sampling). z-lab/Qwen3.6-27B-DFlash and
   our merlin-dflash-ft are plain DFlashDraftModel (greedy argmax draft), so these lines never run for us.
   A selector drafter with this patch is still non-deterministic.
 - Greedy (T=0) needs no coins and is unchanged.
 - Logit numerics: the patch makes the RNG per-request; the logits themselves still depend on batch
   composition (see NOTES.txt / G2_PLAN.txt arm c: --enable-deterministic-inference).
